{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519740-nephandi","id":1519740,"title":"Nephandi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-04T06:44:06-07:00","id":1519740,"title":"Nephandi","content":"So I am planning a project that involves a series of vaguely interconnected chronicles but ultimately share a common plot connection if players know what to pay attention to. The Chronicles will basically hop around each gameline.<br /> <br /> The ultimate big bads? The Nephandi naturally. <br /> <br /> I'm curious, aside from the obvious Nephandi related books, what is some material and ideas to really help with getting into the head of the average Nephandus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:08:57-07:00","id":1519770,"title":"","content":"M20 Book of the Fallen is a strong starting point: <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/294224/M20-Book-of-the-Fallen?term=Book+of+the+\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/4261/294224.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/294224/M20-Book-of-the-Fallen?term=Book+of+the+\" target=\"_blank\"> M20 Book of the Fallen - Onyx Path Publishing | Mage 20th Anniversary | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/294224/M20-Book-of-the-Fallen?term=Book+of+the+\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/294224/M20-Book-of-the-Fallen?term=Book+of+the+ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> M20 Book of the Fallen - Are you predator or prey? For the Nephandi, that&rsquo;s a simple question: They embody the Abyss, and you are their next me </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Although you can create your own pretty easily depending on cosmology, so if your following pure Mage then either an inverse or corrupt anti- version of the Technocracy or Traditions, a mage following one of the cthonic or fallen religions or lean into Lovecraft territory for \u2018Things that man weren\u2019t meant to know\u201d<br /> <br /> Good Old Fashioned Black Magic from Black Druids following the Old Gods to Crowley-esque Black Mass.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s any werewolf influences you have Mage following the Wyrm, Wraith Mage who have fallen to Oblivion and Changeling Mage who has succumbed to The Elder Dark.<br /> <br /> Depending on your campaigns Cosmology the latter may all be different faces of the same being though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:15:54-07:00","id":1519772,"title":"","content":"Did try and post suggesting the Book of the Fallen and a few Homebrew ideas but spam filters snagged it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T11:30:35-07:00","id":1519774,"title":"","content":"I would obviously go for Book of the Fallen as a primary resource. I was thinking more unintuitive ideas I might overlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T13:30:46-07:00","id":1519783,"title":"","content":"The Cults of Cthulhu sourcebook for the current edition of the Call of Cthulhu RPG, maybe.<br /> <br /> If you've never seen them, Clive Barker's Lord of Illusions and John Carpenter's In the Mouth of Madness. Maybe also 1977's Suspiria and 2018's Apostle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-04-2023, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T14:19:35-07:00","id":1519786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519740-nephandi?p=1519783#post1519783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cults of Cthulhu sourcebook for the current edition of the Call of Cthulhu RPG, maybe.<br /> <br /> If you've never seen them, Clive Barker's Lord of Illusions and John Carpenter's In the Mouth of Madness. Maybe also 1977's Suspiria and 2018's Apostle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you. This is the kind of stuff that I am looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T14:55:46-07:00","id":1519789,"title":"","content":"Depending on how much reading you want to do, Victor Lavalle's The Ballad of Black Tom, which is a retelling of Lovecraft's The Horror at Red Hook from a different point of view. Also maybe Alan Moore's very weighty graphic novel From Hell, which presents the Ripper murders as part of an occult ritual to usher in the many horrors of the 20th century. (Avoid the film adaptation as it is so dumbed down and altered as to almost be an adaptation in name only.)<br /> <br /> Filmwise, I'll also add Angel Heart (I feel that there really should be a Nephandus walking around using the almost absurd alias Louis Cypher) and the original version of Hellboy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T19:12:57-07:00","id":1519819,"title":"","content":"Also, you might consider Mage: the Awakening's closest counterpart to the Nephandi, namely the Scelesti. The discussion there about Antinomianism is definitely relevant; and the sections about befouling and otherwise inverting Magic, while increasingly tied to Awakening's notion of Watchtowers, can still be mined for ideas about why a Nephandus might choose to invest their Avatar or corrupt their Focus. <br /> And speaking of that: you might want to look at Prism of Focus, on Storyteller's Vault. It's not particularly about the Nephandi; it's primarily about making Practices clearer and more useful. But it has a section about Corrupted Practices which might be worth a look.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T15:09:50-07:00","id":1520154,"title":"","content":"Reading up H.P Lovecraft could very well give some notions and ideas in regard to the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Another chance and option is exploring and playing demonic, evil, infernal, and dark factions and characters in card games or computer games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T17:48:05-07:00","id":1520164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519740-nephandi?p=1519819#post1519819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you might consider Mage: the Awakening's closest counterpart to the Nephandi, namely the Scelesti. The discussion there about Antinomianism is definitely relevant; and the sections about befouling and otherwise inverting Magic, while increasingly tied to Awakening's notion of Watchtowers, can still be mined for ideas about why a Nephandus might choose to invest their Avatar or corrupt their Focus.<br /> And speaking of that: you might want to look at Prism of Focus, on Storyteller's Vault. It's not particularly about the Nephandi; it's primarily about making Practices clearer and more useful. But it has a section about Corrupted Practices which might be worth a look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with Scelesti as an inspiration is that the outcome of their corruption is heavily tied to Paradox in a way that I gather the Nephandi are not (under an assumption that Paradox is something mages are very concerned by) in cases where they'd just be in it for the power, and are otherwise engaged with the Abyss more in terms of it containing multitudes (or even the premise of freestyling reality), compared to Nephandi just wanting to destroy everything.<br /> <br /> I feel as though Second Edition has emphasized this by really moving away from the portrayal of them as generic evil cultist mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T01:18:39-07:00","id":1520174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519740-nephandi?p=1520164#post1520164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though Second Edition has emphasized this by really moving away from the portrayal of them as generic evil cultist mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>For regular evil Mages, traitors and renegades from the Traditions or Crafts do well enough. The Nephandi do have their own very distinct characterfulness, culture, qualities, attributes, and tendencies.<br /> <br /> For example they believe in the value of hostiltiy and antagonisms.<br /> They are also seekers and scholars of forbidden and dangerous knowledge.<br /> The Nephandi value practice over theory, but they also see the worth in jokes, bravado, charisma, and ideaology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T08:32:19-07:00","id":1520201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1519740-nephandi?p=1520174#post1520174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For regular evil Mages, traitors and renegades from the Traditions or Crafts do well enough. The Nephandi do have their own very distinct characterfulness, culture, qualities, attributes, and tendencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I refer to something as generically evil, I don't mean evil without other distinguishing characteristics, I mean evil as sole or overwhelmingly primary characteristic.<br /> <br /> I can't deny that I feel as though a game as concerned with the cultural and ideological basis and expression of magic as Mage: the Ascension is, the nicest thing that could be said about the Nephandi is that they stick out like a sore thumb. The premise that they exist with an inversion of the impulse for Ascension would kind of alleviate some of the problems in providing an existential basis for their cartoonish supervillainy, but I would think kind of just steps into a follow up question of what really motivates somebody to seek Descension.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T08:46:25-07:00","id":1520205,"title":"","content":"Perhaps <b>Infernalism: The Path of Screams </b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/165/Infernalism-The-Path-of-Screams\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ath-of-Screams</a><br /> <br /> Or Clanbook Baali<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 08-09-2023, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T17:27:18-07:00","id":1520246,"title":"","content":"I might recommend reading <i>The Old Gods Waken</i> by Manly Wade Wellman, <i>The Scream</i> by Craig Spector and John Skipp, and <i>Coldheart Canyon</i> or \u200b&quot;The Last Illusion&quot; by Clive Barker for some inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}